# Allowlist build context: the engine image needs the workspace sources, and
# docs/ — the support agent reads it at runtime as its knowledge base, so it is
# a dependency, not documentation. Everything else (secrets, data, git history,
# installer) stays out.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!packages
packages/**/__pycache__
packages/**/*.egg-info
# A stray runtime directory in a bundled agent's profile: git ignores `data/`,
# so it never shows up in a diff, and without this line it is copied into the
# image of anyone who builds locally after running the engine from the tree.
packages/**/data
!deploy
!docs
